OL,3,GNEWSAPolice work-from-home 'spoofing'
OL,4,Ainvestigation launched
OL,5,
OL,6,FA police investigation has been
OL,7,Flaunched into 21 police officers, staff
OL,8,Fand contractors who are suspected of
OL,9,F"productivity spoofing," Deputy Chief
OL,10,FConstable Bobby Singleton has said.
OL,12,FIn a letter to Policing Board members,
OL,13,FSingleton said Operation Akarpos has
OL,14,Fbeen launched to guard against abuse of
OL,15,Fremote working and to ensure the
OL,16,Fproductivity of staff.
OL,18,FThe Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), who is
OL,19,Fcarrying out the operation, has found
OL,20,F"no systemic abuse of home working by
OL,21,FPSNI officers and staff".
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
